{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/680883-drivethrurpg-print-quality","id":680883,"title":"DriveThruRPG print quality","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-28T04:40:23-07:00","id":680883,"title":"DriveThruRPG print quality","content":"Apologies in advance if this is the wrong place<br /> <br /> I recently ordered two books from said site, as PoD. Dark Ages: Vampire was one of them. Its nice and all, but the paper is relatively thin, and therefore things bleed through. Its sort-of okay with text, but when you have a flipside illustration, you can clearly see it in the background of the text, which is not the best, tbh.<br /> <br /> I have looked at their example pages for standard and premium print quality, and it seems to be that this is an issue with their standard print. I have contacted them, but I'd like to see what others have experienced so far.<br /> <br /> What is your experience?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T07:49:42-07:00","id":680978,"title":"","content":"Correct place but it's been discussed before, the standard printing does have bleed headaches in some situations, it's not an issue at all that I've seen with the premium.<br /> <br /> The different print qualities are what have been made available by the printer, which is mostly aiming books at well... books. When you get into graphics heavy RPG books it shows up a lot more significantly.<br /> <br /> I don't have it handy but I know there have been photo-comparisons showing regular vs premium quality printing with the same book around here in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}